# 6. Independently verify the core frame and pairing architecture

The manuscript places considerable weight on identities of the general form

\[
[M_{X\Theta Y}]
=
\mathsf S_X[\Theta]\mathsf S_Y,
\qquad
\mathsf S_X^2=I,
\]

and

\[
\langle A|[M_{X\Theta Y}]|B\rangle
\equiv
(A\Leftrightarrow X)\Theta(Y\Leftrightarrow B).
\]

Verify these from first principles.

Check their exact algebraic interpretation:

- which multiplication is being used;
- what ring or Boolean algebra entries live in;
- whether the identities hold syntactically or only modulo Boolean equivalence;
- whether they remain valid for arbitrary formulas;
- what assumptions are needed for valuation;
- what happens when formulas are dependent;
- what the pairing means semantically.

Determine whether these identities constitute:

- genuinely new mathematical results;
- novel packaging of classical Boolean expansion;
- a useful representation theorem;
- a change-of-frame formulation;
- or some combination.

Do not prejudge the answer.

