# 23. Standards for the final judgment

A paper is not publication-ready merely because:

- its calculations work on examples;
- an earlier reviewer liked it;
- a previous agent assigned a high score;
- it has many theorem environments;
- it contains extensive supplementary material;
- no counterexample appeared in a small search;
- a novelty search failed to find an exact phrase match.

Likewise, it is not automatically unpublishable because:

- many ingredients are classical;
- some theorems are elementary;
- its contribution is representational or synthetic rather than foundational.

Judge the actual manuscript against the standards appropriate to the contribution it can honestly support.

